<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ruthenians</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ruthenians is the historical name for the East Slavic peoples of the former lands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus'</a>, used especially for the ancestors of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukrainians">Ukrainians</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rusyns">Rusyns</a> living in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a>, Poland-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> monarchy. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> they lived mainly in the north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carpathian-mountains">Carpathians</a>, and in Austrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a> they formed a large, mostly Greek Catholic peasant population.</p></div>
